  "question": {
    "text": "If the co-ordinates of two points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> respectively and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is any point on the conic,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>144</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
